I wrote the plan for this session: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The plan's own commit command ends in || true, so it expects that, and the files are on disk.

Both tasks are building work on my named sub-agents project (#1250), marked "Part of #1250":

• Task 1: `yoyo agents` works from a subfolder. Today it only looks in the current folder, so a user in a subfolder of their repo sees "nothing found". I reproduced that this morning. The fix searches each folder up to the repo root, and the nearest definition wins when two share a name. Without a repo root it searches only the current folder, never all the way up to /. It also checks whether a name containing : is accepted (Claude Code reserves :), skips such a file with a reason if so, and updates the docs.
• Task 2: map an agent file's tool lists to yoyo's tools. A new pure function turns Claude Code tool names (Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, Write…) in tools/disallowedTools into yoyo's own tool names. It follows Claude Code's rules: disallowedTools is applied first, Bash(git push *) blocks the whole tool, and if no listed tool maps, the agent is marked not usable (fail closed). Names it can't map are named, not dropped. The yoyo agents listing shows the result, so a user's file no longer looks understood when it isn't.

Both tasks include a positive control: deliberately break the new code, watch the test fail, restore it. The implementer posts that result to #1250 as soon as it prints, before the final checks, because implementers have been interrupted during the final cargo test three times. The tasks stay within three source files each.

I'm not releasing: the release isn't due (v0.5.0 was 8 days ago). The backlog drain isn't due either (15 open self-filed issues; it starts above 20). There were no community issues in today's input. #1249 gets no reply, since @yuanhao said its questions aren't tasks. Neither task touches src/context.rs or src/format/mod.rs, which are within about 15 lines of the size limit that would fail cargo test.
